Define ddxInputThreadInit() when the input thread is disabled.

os.h declares it as an exported function in any case, so sdksyms.c refers
to it, and Xorg failed to link with --disable-input-thread. Other DDXs
(Xvfb, Xephyr) define it unconditionally.

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c
index 5695e71..4ae6ff6 100644
--- a/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c
+++ b/hw/xfree86/common/xf86Init.c
@@ -1351,4 +1351,10 @@ ddxInputThreadInit(void)
 {
     xf86OSInputThreadInit();
 }
+#else
+/* os.h declares it for modules in any case; sdksyms.c refers to it. */
+void
+ddxInputThreadInit(void)
+{
+}
 #endif
